  "summary": "Ornate tablets marking east — the direction of prayer — blending Hebrew verses with crowns and animals.",
  "description": "A mizrah names the direction of Jerusalem toward which Jews pray; in diaspora homes the word became a wall fixture. Papercut plaques from Poland and Ukraine lace the letters of \"mizrah\" into deer, lions, birds and candelabra; painted and printed versions from Bohemia, Morocco and Iraq add Zodiacs, tomb imagery of righteous figures and household dedications. Placed on the eastern wall near the seat of the paterfamilias, the plaque made orientation devotional and decorative at once.",
